  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Salim Lari @ Salim Zafer Lari vs State Of U.P. on 19 October, 2019 Author: Sudhir Agarwal Bench: Sudhir Agarwal High Court Of Judicature At Allahabad Court No. - 34 Case :- Criminal Revision No. - 7 of 1998 Revisionist :- Salim Lari @ Salim Zafer Lari Opposite Party :- State Of U.P. Counsel for Revisionist :- R.B. Sahai Counsel for Opposite Party :- A.G.A.",
    "facts": "Being aggrieved, appellant has preferred present revision. It is contended that there is no compliance of Section 13(2) of Act, 1954.",
    "arguments": "On the question of compliance of Section 13(2) of Act, 1954, I find that Lower Appellate Court has discussed this issue in para-9 which reads as under:- \"9. , Court has said as under: \"The very purpose of furnishing such report is to enable the Accused to seek for reference to the Central Food Laboratory for analysis if the Accused is dissatisfied with the report.",
